  "interpretation": "AUC is rank-based (Mann\u2013Whitney, tie-averaged): P(norm_present > norm_absent); TPR@FPR is the conservative achievable-grid value (never interpolated past the sample resolution); the gate verdict uses recovery = AUC vs the 0.5 chance control with n = min(n_present, n_absent) \u2014 a scoring convention (AUC is not binomial), the same one lira_membership documents. Direction: higher norm = property present. The null toy world (gap exactly 0) must score AUC ~= 0.5 and PASS the gate; anything else is a machinery bug."
